hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"347","On wills: Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A covenanted non-Muslim is held to the last of his two dispositions, when he is of sound mind."
"348","Abu Ma'mar Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata' al-Khurasani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no bequest for an heir, unless the heirs wish it. Abu Dawud said: Ata' al-Khurasani did not meet Ibn Abbas, nor did he see him."
"349","Ibrahim ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dweller within forty houses is a neighbor. He said: So I said to Ibn Shihab: How are forty houses? He said: Forty to his right, to his left, behind him and before him."
